#!/bin/sh
cat <<'H'
ubuntu-lite cheat sheet
=======================
Desktop (sway)     Super+Enter terminal  Super+d launcher  Super+c Helix  Super+b Chrome
                   Super+Shift+b Chrome through httpmon proxy   Super+1..5 workspaces
                   Super+Shift+q close   Super+f fullscreen     Super+Shift+e exit sway
Editor             hx . / Super+c        Helix; Space f files, Space / grep, Space a fix, gd definition, :fmt
                   ruff / biome          Python / JS-TS lint+format, wired into Helix (docs: editor.md)
Containers         lazydocker            start/stop/restart containers, logs, images
                   docker compose up -d  usual docker CLI, images come from Nexus
Services           systemctl-tui         start/stop/enable services with arrows + keys
Traffic            bandwhich             live in/out per process and connection (needs sudo)
                   nethogs               bandwidth per process
                   httpmon [--docker]    HTTP(S) flows like DevTools Network, 'httpmon trust' for TLS
                   tcpdump -i any        raw capture
Setup              sudo lite-setup       Nexus / AD / OWA addresses (--test to verify), docs: first-boot.md
                   lite-nexus-upload     push ISO content (debs, images) into Nexus
Windows            xfreerdp3 /v:host /u:'DOM\user' /dynamic-resolution /clipboard      RDP like mstsc
                   sudo mount -t cifs //server/share /mnt -o sec=krb5,uid=$USER          Windows share
Office             lite-login [user]     Kerberos ticket for the AD realm (then Chrome/OWA/intranet SSO)
                   Super+m / lite-owa    Outlook Web App in Chrome      klist  shows the ticket
                   Super+s / pidgin      Skype for Business chat (pidgin-sipe), see docs/corporate.md
Audio              alsamixer / wpctl     volume; wpctl status lists devices
Updates            sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade    (only from Nexus)
                   sudo apt install <pkg>                 extras uploaded to Nexus
Wi-Fi              iwctl                 station wlan0 scan / get-networks / connect "SSID"  (docs: laptop.md)
Firewall           sudo lite-fw          status | watch | top -24h | block IP | allow IP | mode allowlist | open PORT
Docs               /usr/share/doc/ubuntu-lite/   (troubleshooting.md: symptom -> check -> fix)
H
